& [ForwardBehaviorMap] is faithful
  + ConsumeInput maps to ProspectiveLane intake of raw impulse as a candidate rather than admitted fact
  + current_focus, current_waist, open_interfaces, admission_records, boundary_constraints, source_refs, and prior artifact ref map to WorkPacket and LaneCursor inputs
  + OpenInterface maps to one named next route with reason, source, exit, and unresolved condition
  + AttachFrame maps to version-bound prepared candidate and source lineage
  + InputDiff maps to requirement, support, meaning, scope, boundary, fault, or neutral MaterialEvent and DiffRecord
  + MeaningDelta maps to semantic change with adopted, candidate, deferred, refused, outside, neutral, or fault status
  + ForwardFrameRecord maps to prospective packet fields and ChangeCapsule declared intent
  + NextSeedEmission maps to bounded reentry state and next work packet
  + NeutralTick maps to optional non-material MicroEvent retained only for liveness or audit need
  + FaultRouting maps to typed lane fault before expansion

& [RearBehaviorMap] is faithful
  + RearReviewInputs map to prior reentry, pulse, commit, declared intent, actual diff, worktree status, source refs, and manager state
  + DeclaredIntent maps to immutable ChangeCapsule intent before inspecting actual results
  + ActualDiff maps to created, updated, deleted, untouched expected, extra-owned, missing, unrelated, neutral, and fault classifications
  + DiffReview maps to backtracking from actual change to prior intent before forming the next seed
  + JustificationDelta maps to supported, overreach, underreach, reordered, blocked, redirected, or no change
  + MeaningDelta, SupportDelta, RequirementDelta, and FaultDelta remain separately represented
  + CompletionClaimGate maps to accept, qualify, repair, block, or unresolved rear disposition input
  + rear review retains power to reject or block a completion claim
  + private chain-of-thought is explicitly excluded as evidence

& [TandemBehaviorMap] is faithful
  + right_commit_created maps to one observed forward result or committed transition boundary
  + forward_packet_emitted maps to durable LaneMessage send record
  + left_packet_received maps to explicit receipt or acknowledgment
  + reflection_packet_returned maps to version-bound ReflectionReturn
  + next_forward_released maps to ObserverJoin release of only the named dependent slice
  + fault_timeout_or_missing_ack maps to typed timeout, missing receipt, missing return, and residual state
  + required order maps to causal predecessor and state-transition constraints
  + checker refusal maps to release barrier failure
  + optional timer maps only to bounded handshake timeout, not work pacing
  + message sending and runner mutation remain absent in the reviewed controller

& [ReentryBehaviorMap] is faithful
  + frame identity maps to lane, capsule, plan, and repository generation identities
  + current focus and attention keys map to bounded subject and query criteria
  + functional description maps to TaskContract purpose and WorkPacket scope
  + source refs map to content-bound provenance
  + backward reflection ref maps to exact ReflectionReturn and reviewed capsule generation
  + resistance and interference notes map to objections, uncertainty, residual, and faults
  + next attention seed maps to next WorkPacket only after applicable Observer release
  - never: use reentry as a second hidden memory store

& [DeclaredDeviations] preserve CTPR's different scope
  + CTPR replaces project-specific frame IDs and thread IDs with stable general task, lane, capsule, and generation UUIDs
  + CTPR separates prospective preparation from physical execution, while the Walking Attention right-foot metaphor sometimes associates forward work with a commit boundary
  + CTPR makes Observer the general admission join rather than treating the reflection packet alone as release authority
  + CTPR generalizes target files and Git diffs into physical, source, semantic, build, behavioral, effect, proof, and calendar diff surfaces
  + CTPR permits only explicitly profiled bounded lag; the reviewed core exchange requires reflection before named next release
  + CTPR defines future message transport abstractly; the selected external controller explicitly implements no sending
  + CTPR derives no live calendar, provider, compiler, background, or effect capability from Walking Attention
  + CTPR does not import the external repository's 584 unrelated dirty entries

& [NonImportSet] is mandatory
  + hidden model attention
  + private chain-of-thought
  + K/V cache or activation access
  + raw attention heatmaps
  + consciousness or persistent subjective state
  + one-minute or fixed pulse work pacing
  + shared mutable attention across models
  + unrestricted executor or runner mutation authority
  + automatic message sending
  + automatic Git commit or workspace mutation
  + prompt-strengthening artifacts as release authority
  + external dirty worktree content outside the selected clean files

& [FidelityAcceptance] passes at behavioral-source grade
  + source repository, branch, HEAD, commit time, dirty count, bytes, hashes, and selected-file clean state are recorded
  + forward input, diff, meaning, fault, frame, and reentry behavior have explicit CTPR destinations
  + rear intent, actual diff, delta, fault, completion, and refusal behavior have explicit CTPR destinations
  + tandem send, receive, return, release, timeout, and no-hidden-state behavior have explicit CTPR destinations
  + deviations and non-imports are explicit
  + external signature status is reported accurately as unsigned candidate
  + CTPR may canonically articulate its own derived behavior after SJS but does not claim to inherit an external valid signature

& [InvalidationAndRecheck] is fail-closed
  + external HEAD change
  + selected file byte or hash change
  + selected file becomes dirty, removed, untracked, or superseded
  + external controller signature status or source lineage changes
  + CTPR changes any mapped forward, rear, tandem, reentry, admission, or non-import behavior

